      "components": ["T3", "T5"],
      "pins": ["T3.1", "T3.2", "T3.3", "T5.1", "T5.2", "T5.3"],
      "nets": ["/+24V_{F}", "+24V", "/G_{RPP}", "/G_{ATO}", "/D_{ATO}", "ATO_VALVE", "GND"],
      "observed": "T3 is populated as a P-channel MOSFET (AON6407, P-CH) with its source tied to /+24V_{F}, drain tied to +24V, and gate tied to /G_{RPP} (a 33 kΩ pull-up to /+24V_{F} and a 12 V Zener to GND). It is not connected to the ATO_VALVE control net. The ATO valve low-side switching is instead done by T5 (AO3400A N-channel MOSFET), whose gate is driven from /G_{ATO} through R10/R12 and T4.",
      "expected": "The specification states that T3 is an AON6407 N-channel MOSFET used as the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch, with its gate driven through R10 from the ESP32 ATO_VALVE pin and pre-driven by T4.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"T3\") (value \"AON6407\") ... (libsource (lib \"Coert-Vonk\") (part \"MOSFET P-CH 30V 32A 10m\u03a9 AON6407\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/+24V_{F}\") ... (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"+24V\") ... (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"72\") (name \"ATO_VALVE\") (node (ref \"M1\") (pin \"J1_12\") ... ) (node (ref \"R10\") (pin \"1\") ... ))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch | Netlist: drives ATO_VALVE net; gate driven through R10 (100 \u03a9), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve path is not implemented as described in the specification. T3 behaves as a fixed-biased P-channel high-side 24 V switch/protection device rather than a GPIO-controlled low-side ATO switch, while T5 performs the low-side switching. This changes the intended actuation topology and could affect ATO control, protection behavior, and component ratings.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist supports one main anomaly: T3 is a P-channel MOSFET wired as a fixed-biased high-side 24 V switch, not the N-channel ATO-valve low-side switch described in the specification; ATO switching is instead done by T5."
}

